{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat ../final_evaluation/invocation.json; sed -n '45,52p' paper.sty; cat ../task/requirements.txt; sed -n '1,70p' ../task/task_contract.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"evaluator_sha256\": \"sha256:9b92407a557f3254b7b5669ae28d9ff03dc160eee38964c6951cc8cbafc829c5\",\n  \"program_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:d566dbc8e195fa324a33bf02f2c26e6c662797861c770832e9b4e90da2f9a48e\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-11-12T23:42:23.063071+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"started\",\n  \"task_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:f8db8afaf5255b318065994c98b90e437410a5250bc069da3c952f9a697568f1\"\n}\n%\\topmargin 0.125in\n\\topmargin -0.625in\n\\addtolength{\\headsep}{0.25in}\n\\textheight 9.0 true in       % Height of text (including footnotes & figures)\n\\textwidth 5.5 true in        % Width of text line.\n\\widowpenalty=10000\n\\clubpenalty=10000\n\nnumpy==2.2.6\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"4c10abc4174a1571188346a912fe8e964e9b391456731d553885fbbfa1b3333b\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Missingness-aware benchmark selection and held-out score prediction\",\n    \"description\": \"Scientific workload: pinned real MTEB embedding-model score matrices, not generative-LLM evaluations. Fixed 48-column task/language/split/primary-metric/dataset-revision panels; natural missingness; k=[1,2,4,8]; eight never-queryable audit columns; >=4 recorded audit cells and >=8 unqueried recorded cells at k=8. Two cases (model-group and name-defined-family-disjoint), three seeds, original/permuted arms, then one REQUIRED zero-weight reset-replay diagnostic episode, 13 episodes total. No optional additional replay is permitted. Search has 24 held-out rows and 73-76 historical rows; final has 48 held-out rows and 88-99 historical rows. Smoke has one case, 24 historical rows, two held-out rows, 16 columns, four audit columns and k=[1,2]; its three episodes are original, permuted, required replay. Supply workload dimensions/checkpoints through inputs, never through seeds.\\nData policy: a fixed English task allowlist is curated from actual pinned source documents, selecting the revision with most allowlisted documents per source model (lexicographic revision tie-break). Before feature extraction, canonicalize complete raw JSON with sorted keys; Unicode NFC, CRLF->LF, per-line trailing whitespace removal; integer-valued floats canonicalized to integers and nonfinite raw measurements represented explicitly as null. Remove identity/runtime-only keys evaluation_time, kg_co2_emissions, mteb_version, model_name, model, model_id, model_revision, revision, timestamp, path, evaluation_time_per_sample, dataset_revision, dataset_id, date. Canonicalize mteb_dataset_name to task_name. Preserve complete score-bearing payloads and task/dataset context. Hash each complete normalized document and each complete raw document-set row independently of source ID; union rows sharing any such hash, then assign components deterministically by SHA256(sorted source IDs joined with | plus split-v1), sorted component index modulo five: 0/1 search, others final. Filter only raw-document coverage >=16 before partition. Verified normalized raw-document/row hash intersections empty; frozen per-plane SHA256 embeds this joint audited split without placing final hashes in search resources. Runtime rechecks its own artifact/document/row hashes and train/test identity/content disjointness. Preserve original raw-source byte checksums and source paths as provenance, not as RPC inputs. Only historical coverage selects panel/audit membership; test eligibility uses masks, never values/errors. Classification accuracy, clustering v_measure, retrieval ndcg_at_10 and reranking map have fixed [0,1] bounds; signed Spearman correlations map (x+1)/2. A present main_score must agree within 1e-5 with the declared primary metric. Incompatible dataset revisions remain distinct columns; no held-out extrema, imputed targets or leaderboard aggregates.\\nMethod and limits: starter and native random-lowrank baseline actually execute masked alternating ridge factorization with historical-only 10% cell validation over ranks 2/4 and ridge 0.1/1, eight sweeps per validation fit, then 30 full-history fit sweeps. Starter selects by maximum latent posterior variance and ridge-conditions on each permitted acquired score. Native random-lowrank uses seeded random acquisition and the same true factorization/conditioning, not an alias. Separate correlation-cover baseline uses overlapping historical pairwise correlations shrunk by n/(n+10), greedy squared-correlation coverage and masked per-target ridge regression with mean-centered zero-imputation of missing predictors, fixed ridge 0.1. Historical means and observed-score copying are separate evaluator-owned constant/copy controls on the candidate's matched target sets. CPU-only NumPy suffices for these methods and alternatives in the canonical research scope. Internal sweep counts are advisory, not candidate-reported validity evidence. Evaluator validates legal selections, observed values, bounded predictions, matched controls and replay; it cannot prove inaccessible candidate internals. Source/mathematical method verification is additional publication evidence, never a self-report flag.\\nControls frozen before scoring: historical means invariant under within-column observed-value derangements; copying depends only on authorized observed-score mean; useful cross-task advantage is hypothesized (not required) to attenuate under independently destroyed alignment; reset replay must reproduce selections and float32 predictions within absolute 1e-6. The actual candidate method runs both history arms, with identical seed, metadata, targets, masks, acquisition budgets and work allowance; no arm label crosses RPC. Construct nonidentity index derangements separately for every nonconstant historical column, verify actual value changes, identical marginal multisets/missing masks and at least two distinct effective mappings; reject constant/no-op controls. No claim follows from an incomplete control or positive penalty-induced gap. No adaptivity gate is added: observation-independent benchmark selection is legal.\\nAggregation fixed before execution: target cells equally within model; model-group case models equally; family case models equally within each held-out name-family, then families equally. Average k equally (1/4 production, 1/2 smoke), seeds equally (1/3 production), cases equally (1/2 production). These linear fixed weights commute, and the implementation computes k-within-model before fixed family averaging. Baseline own acquisitions define its unqueried set; constant/copy share candidate selections. Common audit-panel per-model/k losses are retained in evaluator-owned evidence for matched-target comparisons. Original episodes define candidate and baseline MAEs; permuted episodes define permuted_mae; permutation_gap=permuted_mae-candidate_mae is descriptive only. combined_score=1-candidate_mae. Replay has zero score weight. Any failed entire episode or required baseline/control retains all five losses=1 at its full predeclared weight, never omitted/renormalized; missing replay fails validity. Evidence records one aggregate record per seed, including all cases/arms/failures and measured durations. Its solution fields are evaluator-owned observations, not candidate assertions. Runtime is not a scored metric and no canonical productive-work minimum exists.\\nRPC operation table per episode: reset=1, upload_start=1, upload_chunk=8 maximum, upload_commit=1, fit=1, row_start=R, observe=8R. Row-start selects the first benchmark; each observe returns the next selection and checkpoint prediction. Total=12+9R. Search R=24 gives 228*13=2964; final R=48 gives 444*13=5772. This same complete total is enforced by the evaluator and harness. Setup and commit are counted even with one actual chunk. Smoke R=2,kmax=2 gives (12+3R)*3=54 maximum; actual chunks may be fewer. No download/state-export operations exist. Matrix logical cap=32MiB, max_chunks=8, decoded chunk cap=4MiB, contiguous offsets, <f4 values plus uint8 masks, full prediction <=128 float32 entries. All transfer state is candidate-owned memory, never shared paths. Preflight actually serializes maximum-shape matrix requests, a maximum base64 chunk, reset/row/observe metadata and maximum response with compact UTF-8 JSON plus newline, a representative JSON RPC envelope and an additional 65536-byte framing/envelope reserve. All complete messages remain strictly below 67108864 bytes. Maximum-count protocol mock traces verify all 13 episodes against the operation table with eight valid subchunks per upload. Wire schema/integrity is separate from scientific claims.\\nScheduling/resources: one monotonic invocation deadline from module startup, minus conservative broker/container startup reserve 60s search/90s final, and finalization reserve 20s. Three sequential productive methods per episode (random-lowrank, correlation-ridge, candidate) each reserve 15s search/30s final plus 1s cleanup; resets and dispatch/cleanup reserve 4s per episode globally, including diagnostic replay. Joint bounds: search=60+20+13*(4+3*(15+1))=756s<900; final=90+20+13*(4+3*(30+1))=1371s<1800. Smoke reserves 15s startup, 5s finalization, 5s per productive method and the same isolated paths, <=120s. RPC reset bound 2s; non-reset work is capped by method and global deadlines. Failed episodes continue remaining declared resets when transport survives. Native subprocess TERM wait .2s + KILL/reap .2s + bounded stderr drain .4s, with 2s episode overhead; baselines are bounded native evaluator loops, not subprocesses. Fake-clock tests exercise near-limit responses, mid-operation/reset timeouts and slow cleanup without starving resets or outputs. Baseline timing excludes reset/startup/import/output; no timeout penalty certifies productive completion. Native mode uses a fresh allowlisted environment, Python from TASK_PYTHON (sys.executable only when unset), shell=False, separate copied code (32MiB/2048 entries/5s bounded source copy), no-network seccomp, read-only Landlock ABI>=3 runtime/code allowlists, CPU affinity (1 evaluator/3 candidate), 8GiB address spaces, aggregate-thread CPU limits and kill/reap. Resolve interpreter command names before runtime allowlisting. Broker mode requires BOTH exact /broker-code/candidate_proxy.py and a nonempty AGENTIC_CANDIDATE_SOCKET, imports/calls only trusted handle in-process, with no child launch or peer telemetry. Production container isolation/all-thread accounting is harness-owned; no invented telemetry API. Linux x86_64 CPython3.11-3.13 supported; draft-tested CPython3.12.15 and NumPy2.2.6 manylinux wheel verified against PyPI metadata and installed offline in a temporary venv. No TeX toolchain or conference template is supplied as an inference dependency; downstream manuscript production must provision official latest-edition assets and compile PDF offline.\\nSeparate predicates: search correct means own frozen-source/content/split checks, all scheduled episodes/baselines/canonical controls completed legally, exact reset transcript, finite bounded predictions, effective permutation, matched budgets and successful required reset replay. There is NO comparative search threshold or bounded calibration delegation in task.md; losing to any baseline or a nonpositive permutation gap is not a search veto. Final correct uses the same validity predicates on the sealed independent pool, NOT a publication-superiority threshold. Operational qualification feasible additionally requires ordinary non-smoke production completion in budget, independent of scientific competitiveness and replay agreement; qualification is emitted only for exact AGENTIC_TASK_QUALIFICATION=1. Publication claim assessment is separate: null/negative/conditional results are legitimate, superiority needs complete paired model/family-cluster uncertainty versus both random-lowrank and correlation-ridge on all-unqueried and common audit targets, multiplicity accounted for or exploratory labels, and supported control evidence. Never conclude learning from a changed state hash or schema-valid self-report.\\nBest-shot limitations: family annotation is an explicit name-defined lineage/owner proxy from source model IDs, not an independently verified genealogical separation; restrict corresponding claims. Fixed English-panel selection and recorded-entry availability induce coverage/MNAR bias. Cellwise historical validation is not a guarantee for family shift. The scaffold does not assert novelty, complete literature review, a causal mechanism, a universal sufficient k, generative-model generalization, a finished paper, conference compliance or completed scientific research. Those remain documented downstream evidence obligations. No forbidden-paper search was performed; only named MTEB source and authoritative NumPy package metadata were accessed.\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_recorded_scores\",\n      \"search_controls\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_recorded_scores\",\n      \"final_controls\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_recorded_scores\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"candidate_mae\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_recorded_scores\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"historical_mean_mae\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_recorded_scores\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"observed_copy_mae\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_recorded_scores\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"random_lowrank_mae\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_recorded_scores\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"greedy_ridge_mae\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_recorded_scores\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"permuted_mae\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_controls\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"permutation_gap\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_controls\"\n      },\n      {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
