{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_137","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/paper-venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport pymupdf,re\np=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\nfor idx in [7,8,11]:\n t=p[idx].get_text();print('PAGE',idx+1);print(t[:1300]);print(t[-900:])\nPY\nsed -n '1,90p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\"","aggregated_output":"PAGE 8\n378\n379\n380\n381\n382\n383\n384\n385\n386\n387\n388\n389\n390\n391\n392\n393\n394\n395\n396\n397\n398\n399\n400\n401\n402\n403\n404\n405\n406\n407\n408\n409\n410\n411\n412\n413\n414\n415\n416\n417\n418\n419\n420\n421\n422\n423\n424\n425\n426\n427\n428\n429\n430\n431\nThe control cannot distinguish shared capability from correlated reporting, benchmark overlap, or\nother joint structure in the historical table. It also does not simulate a realistic future distribution\nshift. Its purpose is narrower: after destroying observed alignment while retaining column marginals\nand the missingness mask, the recorded predictive accuracy deteriorates. The deliberately weak\nqueried-score-average reference and deterministic replay are reported separately in Supplementary\nInformation rather than treated as competing explanations of the main comparison.\n6\nDISCUSSION AND LIMITATIONS\nWhat the comparison establishes.\nThe evidence supports lower aggregate error for the frozen\nLATENT procedure than for the two executed predictive baselines on these recorded English em-\nbedding panels. The common-target comparison strengthens this finding because scored audit cells\ndo not change with acquisition. It remains a comparison among evaluated complete configurations.\nIn particular, the data do not establish that mixtures were selected, that a mixture outperforme\ns-aware latent pro-\ncedure obtains lower aggregate normalized absolute error than random-acquisition low-rank and\ngreedy-coverage ridge pipelines.\nIts advantage persists on never-queryable audit targets, but a\nfamily-disjoint split favors ridge, and historical-column permutation substantially increases error.\nThe appropriate conclusion is thus a bounded empirical finding about complete configurations, not\nuniform superiority or identification of a successful component. The method supplies an explicit\nobserved-data model, conditional predictions, and a historical-only selection procedure; the evi-\ndence leaves realized mixture use, acquisition causality, and prospective calibration unresolved.\nWithin the tested budgets, additional observations improve descriptive mean audit accuracy, but the\nstudy does not determine a universally adequate number of benchmarks. Retaining common targets,\n8\n\nPAGE 9\n432\n433\n434\n435\n436\n437\n438\n439\n440\n441\n442\n443\n444\n445\n446\n447\n448\n449\n450\n451\n452\n453\n454\n455\n456\n457\n458\n459\n460\n461\n462\n463\n464\n465\n466\n467\n468\n469\n470\n471\n472\n473\n474\n475\n476\n477\n478\n479\n480\n481\n482\n483\n484\n485\nadverse splits, and the distinction between recorded and naturally missing scores is essential when\nusing such predictions to reduce evaluation effort.\n9\n\n432\n433\n434\n435\n436\n437\n438\n439\n440\n441\n442\n443\n444\n445\n446\n447\n448\n449\n450\n451\n452\n453\n454\n455\n456\n457\n458\n459\n460\n461\n462\n463\n464\n465\n466\n467\n468\n469\n470\n471\n472\n473\n474\n475\n476\n477\n478\n479\n480\n481\n482\n483\n484\n485\nadverse splits, and the distinction between recorded and naturally missing scores is essential when\nusing such predictions to reduce evaluation effort.\n9\n\nPAGE 12\n594\n595\n596\n597\n598\n599\n600\n601\n602\n603\n604\n605\n606\n607\n608\n609\n610\n611\n612\n613\n614\n615\n616\n617\n618\n619\n620\n621\n622\n623\n624\n625\n626\n627\n628\n629\n630\n631\n632\n633\n634\n635\n636\n637\n638\n639\n640\n641\n642\n643\n644\n645\n646\n647\nA\nSUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION\nA.1\nOBSERVED-DATA MODEL AND NUMERICAL SETTINGS\nThe preserved implementation is provided as readable files in source_evidence/latent/.\nThe factor fitting routine is covariance.py:18; Gaussian conditioning, off-diagonal trans-\nfer, and conditional covariance updates begin at covariance.py:82, covariance.py:97,\nand covariance.py:112.\nThe mixture fit, row conditioning, acquisition, prediction,\nand historical selection are in mixture.py:32, mixture.py:135, mixture.py:164,\nmixture.py:179, and mixture.py:253. These files substantiate implementation descrip-\ntions, not isolated performance claims.\nThe Gaussian candidates use ranks {2, 4, 8} and residual shrinkage {2, 12}. Historical row valida-\ntion reserves min(32, max(2, ⌊M/5⌋)) rows and marks max(1, ⌊N/3⌋) randomly ordered columns\nas internal audit targets. At least six usable validation rows are required for extended selection. Can-\ndidate validation fits use at most twelve sweeps; the supplied final fit uses thirty. Standardization\nhas a scale floor of 0.02; standardized residual variance is f\nsponding evaluator contains\nreadable extraction and disjointness checks. It does not justify unmeasured claims about the full\nupstream leaderboard population.\nIdentity grouping canonicalizes score-bearing source documents, removes identity/runtime meta-\ndata, and checks normalized document and complete-row content. Rows sharing normalized content\nare grouped before the frozen development/final partition. In the family-disjoint condition, held-out\nname-proxy families are also excluded from the historical matrix. The retained final panels have\nbetween 88 and 99 historical rows, depending on split. Each held-out row supplies enough recorded\nentries for the query budget and at least four recorded audit cells. This availability-based filtering ex-\ncludes very sparse target rows. It does not assume that the remaining unrecorded scores are missing\nat random or provide ground truth for them.\n12\n\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate rendered Supplementary Information in a compiled paper PDF.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef _letter_spaced_word_pattern(word: str) -> str:\n    return r\"[ \\t]*\".join(re.escape(character) for character in word)\n\n\nSUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    rf\"(?mi)^[ \\t]*(?:(?:appendix[ \\t]+)?[A-Z0-9]+(?:\\.\\d+)*[.:]?[ \\t]+)?\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('supplementary')}[ \\t]+\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('information')}[ \\t]*$\",\n)\nREFERENCE_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    rf\"(?mi)^[ \\t]*(?:{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('references')}|\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('bibliography')})[ \\t]*$\"\n)\n\n\ndef parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Validate rendered Supplementary Information in a PDF.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--pdf\", required=True)\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef validate_rendered_supplementary_information(page_texts: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    supplement_page_index = next(\n        (\n            index\n            for index, page_text in enumerate(page_texts)\n            if SUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE.search(page_text)\n        ),\n        None,\n    )\n    if supplement_page_index is None:\n        return [\"compiled paper is missing the Supplementary Information heading\"]\n\n    heading_page_text = page_texts[supplement_page_index]\n    heading_match = SUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE.search(heading_page_text)\n    assert heading_match is not None\n    reference_page_indices = [\n        index\n        for index, page_text in enumerate(page_texts[:supplement_page_index])\n        if REFERENCE_HEADING_RE.search(page_text)\n    ]\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    if not reference_page_indices:\n        errors.append(\"compiled paper is missing the References heading before SI\")\n    heading_page_prefix = heading_page_text[: heading_match.start()]\n    prefix_lines = [line.strip() for line in heading_page_prefix.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n    earlier_header_lines = {\n        line.strip()\n        for page_text in page_texts[:supplement_page_index]\n        for line in page_text.splitlines()[:2]\n        if line.strip()\n    }\n    substantive_prefix_lines = [\n        line\n        for line in prefix_lines\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"(?:page\\s+)?\\d+\", line, re.IGNORECASE) is None\n        and line not in earlier_header_lines\n    ]\n    if substantive_prefix_lines:\n        errors.append(\n            \"compiled Supplementary Information must start on a separate page after References\"\n        )\n\n    supplement_chunks = [\n        heading_page_text[heading_match.end() :],\n        *page_texts[supplement_page_index + 1 :],\n    ]\n    substantive_chunks: list[str] = []\n    for chunk in supplement_chunks:\n        later_references = REFERENCE_HEADING_RE.search(chunk)\n        if later_references is not None:\n            substantive_chunks.append(chunk[: later_references.start()])\n            break\n        substantive_chunks.append(chunk)\n    supplement_text = \"\\n\".join(substantive_chunks)\n    visible_character_count = len(re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", supplement_text).strip())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
