{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_145","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/paper-tools/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-Budgeted benchmark prediction requires evaluating both a selection policy and the predictor it enables. On naturally incomplete English MTEB panels, the studied missingness-aware latent procedure obtains lower aggregate normalized absolute error than random-acquisition low-rank and greedy-coverage ridge pipelines. Its advantage persists on never-queryable audit targets, but a family-disjoint split favors ridge, and historical-column permutation substantially increases error. The appropriate conclusion is thus a bounded empirical finding about complete configurations, not uniform superiority or identification of a successful component. The method supplies an explicit observed-data model, conditional predictions, and a historical-only selection procedure; the evidence leaves realized mixture use, acquisition causality, and prospective calibration unresolved. Within the tested budgets, additional observations improve descriptive mean audit accuracy, but the study does not determine a universally adequate number of benchmarks. Retaining common targets, adverse splits, and the distinction between recorded and naturally missing scores is essential when using such predictions to reduce evaluation effort.\n+Budgeted benchmark prediction requires evaluating both a selection policy and the predictor it enables. On naturally incomplete English MTEB panels, the studied missingness-aware latent procedure obtains lower aggregate normalized absolute error than random-acquisition low-rank and greedy-coverage ridge pipelines. Its advantage persists on never-queryable audit targets, but a family-disjoint split favors ridge, and historical-column permutation substantially increases error. The appropriate conclusion is thus a bounded empirical finding about complete configurations, not uniform superiority or identification of a successful component. Within the tested budgets, additional observations improve descriptive mean audit accuracy, but the study does not determine a universally adequate number of benchmarks. Retaining common targets, adverse splits, and the distinction between recorded and naturally missing scores is essential when using such predictions to reduce evaluation effort.\n@@\n The Gaussian limit preserves the clipped conditional-mean predictor. If mixture fitting fails numerically, the final refit restores the Gaussian. The implementation also computes internal matched comparisons, but the external evidence does not verify their numerical outputs. Accordingly, we report neither those comparisons nor inferred component preferences as completed ablations.\n+\n+The implementation maintains dense benchmark-by-benchmark conditional covariances, requiring \"'$O(N''^2)$ row-state storage and an $O(N''^2)$ rank-one update after each query. Fitting adds repeated historical-model solves and multiple validation configurations. This is a CPU-only implementation for the retained panels, not an established scalable solution for arbitrarily large benchmark collections. No measured training-time or benchmark-execution saving is claimed.\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/latent/mixture.py#MixtureRow.reveal]]\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/latent/covariance.py#reveal_covariance]]\n*** Update File: finalize_references.py\n@@\n-            venue = (crossref.get('\"'container-title') or [data.get('venue') or 'Technical report'])[0]\n+            location_source = (data.get('primary_location') or {}).get('source') or {}\n+            venue = (crossref.get('container-title') or [data.get('venue') or location_source.get('display_name') or 'Technical report'])[0]\n@@\n-        entry_type = 'article'\n+        title = BeautifulSoup(title, 'html.parser').get_text(' ', strip=True)\n+        entry_type = 'article'\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-venv/bin/pip install beautifulsoup4 requests >> /tmp/paper-install.log 2>&1 && /tmp/paper-venv/bin/pip freeze > requirements-paper.txt\n/tmp/paper-venv/bin/python finalize_references.py\n/tmp/paper-venv/bin/python build_claim_mapping.py\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
